The high-spin to low-spin switch for octahedral d⁵ happens at **Dq ≈ 1 792 cm⁻¹** (Δ = 10·Dq ≈ 17 918 cm⁻¹, Dq/B ≈ 2.89).

I computed this with the spin-crossover tool at B = 621 cm⁻¹ and C = 2 851 cm⁻¹. Below the crossing the ground term is the high-spin ⁶A₁; above it, the low-spin ²T₂ becomes the ground state. The two ground-term curves cross at the value above.

